---
title: Orange Pan-Glazed Tempeh
description: Tempeh pan-fried until golden, then simmered in orange juice and ginger until it reduces to a glaze.
tags: [one-pan]
course: main
icons: [citrus, pan-frying, garlic]
author: Jude Blereau
source:
  name: Coming Home to Eat
  url: https://www.101cookbooks.com/panglazed-tempeh-recipe
servings: 2
prep time: 10m
cook time: 20m
difficulty: easy
---

Pour the @orange juice{1%cup}(freshly squeezed, from 3 to 4 large oranges) into a #small bowl{}. Squeeze the @fresh ginger{1%tbsp}(grated) over the bowl so its juice runs in, then discard the pulp. Stir in the @tamari{2%tsp}(or soy sauce), @mirin{1 1/2%tbsp}, @maple syrup{2%tsp}, @ground coriander{1/2%tsp} and @garlic cloves{2}(small, crushed). Set aside.

Cut the @tempeh{283%g}(about 10 oz) into thin, bite-size pieces.

Heat the @coconut oil{2%tbsp}(or ghee or olive oil) in a large #frying pan{} over medium-high heat until hot but not smoking. Add the tempeh and fry for ~fry{5%minutes}, until golden underneath. Turn the pieces and fry the other side for another ~fry{5%minutes}, until golden.

Pour the orange juice mixture into the pan and simmer for ~simmer{10%minutes}, until the sauce reduces to a thick glaze. Turn the tempeh once along the way and spoon the sauce over it now and then.

Drizzle the tempeh with any sauce left in the pan, squeeze the @lime{1/2} over it and scatter the @fresh cilantro{1%handful}(leaves) on top.

> **Swaps** — Extra-firm tofu works in place of the tempeh. Pat it dry with a paper towel after cutting.

> **Serving** — Heidi Swanson served this over leftover wheat berries warmed with a few handfuls of chopped kale.
